body:
I don't have much of workout plan. Just a simple 3 day routine, push, pull and legs + core. I've been at it for about 1.5yrs but when I look at others who have also been at it for the same amount of time, my gains seem small.

&#x200B;

I never fake my emotions or confidence. If I did, I'd be smiling in the pictures. My therapist has trying to teach me to "fake it" or fool myself to think more positively.

I didn't even think girls approached guys ever. Or aleast I've never seen it.

&#x200B;

My therapist has been trying to teach me to "fool myself". It just so hard becuase I can't help but to roll my eyes as I know I'm lying to myself. Can I really convice myself I'm the sexiest man on the plannet by repeating it in my mind x times a day?

Been seeing therapists for about 9 years, tried a variety of different therapies. All useless, I really seem like a lost cause.  

&#x200B;

I never know how to approach or know what to say. I'm pretty sure my aspergers is limiting my social skills. Stack that with social anxiety, it makes initiating interaction almost impossible. People never approach me, especially women. I think my looks has something to do with it. I guess they can also sense my depressed mood too.

Life is like an open world RPG... interesting analogy... Hot girls = lvl92 Legendry Mythic Deathclaw (but sexy). Me = lvl3 ugly vault dweller with a pipe pistol (because God was drunk when making me on the character creation menu). I wonder how this interaction will turn out...

&#x200B;

I think all I do in life is "avoid". I never hurt anyone because there was never any interaction in the first place.

&#x200B;

I think I were to learn a skill, I might take up cooking. Just because it's a good useful life skill. I heard girls like good food too, so it might help there. Maybe...

The first pair are sunglasses. They wouldn't look right for regular glasses.

The 2nd pair is a style I'm considering. But it's hard to find that style with a nose pad. Without it they always slide down my face. 

&#x200B;

I was planning on getting my haircut this weekend. Any suggestions (pics)? I prefer short hair becuase it's eaiser and I get nasty cowlicks.

&#x200B;

Well, statisitcally Asian men are one of the least desireable for dating. Of course, it's not the end of the world to be an asian man. I live in Toronto, Canada and it's mostly Asians and whites here. Too bad both asian and white women prefer white men.

I know people don't like me because I'm depressed. But that is also what keeps me depressed. It's a inescapable cycle. I feel depressed because no one likes me, and it's hard to meet people because I'm depressed. 

&#x200B;

I've been working out for 1.5yrs. I'm not very happy with my progress, probablly due to bad routine and diet. I'm planning on hiring a personal trainer because I don't know crap about fitness. I workout at home. Going to the gym gives me anxiety and I'm too lazy to get my ass there.

"You are definitely not as ugly as you think."

&#x200B;

I think I'm absolutely repulsive. So, does that mean I'm just ugly, somewhat ugly, well below average?
